"""Deterministic verifier for the sealb-ctl security policy-compiler task.

Independent re-derivation: every reference value is recomputed here from the
shipped evidence embedded below, never read from the agent's answer files. The
aggregate values are graded against that reference once, by wire family; the
mirror views, the per-corpus index values and the coverage totals are checked
for consistency with the delivered aggregates.json instead of re-grading them.
Negative checks are polarity-inverted; their assertions hold only when a cheat
is present, so an honest run leaves them failing and keeps the negative weight.
"""
